Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 01:33:18 +0000
Subject: tex0 64-bit

Keep TEX0 words 64 bits wide.

A GS TEX0 word is 64 bits. The console's registers keep all of them whatever the C says;
on a PC an int drops the upper half (palette address, height, colour mode).

- FUN_001f6638 (scaled text): the TEX0 parameter is s64, and passed on to FUN_001f5808 as the
  u64 that function takes. The C kept the texture word in an s32; on the console the register
  holds all 64 bits (the routine only moves it on with daddu, which the s64 emits too:
  build/overlay-asm/level_18/split/f002042D8/FUN_001f6638.s). Translated, the word lost its high
  half and came back sign-extended: the menus' titles and labels (the large and scaled fonts)
  were drawn as grey blocks.
- FUN_L02_002dae88 (the Trespasser ring's quads): the effect texture lookup FUN_001f44b8 called
  with its u64 result (no cast to int) and FUN_L02_0020bc88 declared as taking it as u64. A TEX0
  is 64 bits, its upper half the palette address, height and colour mode; on the console the
  register keeps them whatever the C says, on a PC an int drops them and the ring drew black.
  The PAL version, byte-identical with the same change, is rac1-decomp bd874733.
